1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,630
One night, a lake killed
more than 1,700 people,

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,550
and almost none of them
were even in the water.

3
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:10,510
August 21st, 1986,

4
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,880
Cameroon.

5
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:13,710
Families were living peacefully

6
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:16,690
near a beautiful lake called Lake Nyos.

7
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,850
But that night, something
terrifying happened.

8
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,890
An enormous invisible cloud
began spreading from the lake,

9
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,330
flowing down into nearby villages.

10
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,050
People suddenly collapsed.

11
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,510
Animals dropped to the
ground, and by morning,

12
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:34,250
entire communities had been devastated.

13
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:36,250
But here's the strange part.

14
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,930
There was no fire, no
lava, and no visible sign

15
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,330
of what had killed them.

16
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,330
So what actually happened?

17
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,190
Scientists eventually discovered
something extraordinary.

18
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:49,830
Deep beneath the lake, enormous amounts

19
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:53,110
of carbon dioxide had been
building up for years.

20
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:56,750
And on that night, the
trapped gas suddenly escaped.

21
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,830
A deadly cloud swept into the valleys,

22
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,750
filling the air with dangerous
concentrations of carbon dioxide.

23
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:07,830
More than 1,700 people lost their lives.

24
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,110
But here's what makes this
story even more disturbing.

25
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,610
Just two years earlier, another lake

26
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,210
in Cameroon had released deadly gas.

27
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:20,390
37 people died, and almost
nobody imagined that something

28
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,290
far worse was coming.

29
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:25,870
After the disaster, engineers
installed special pipes

30
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,390
to release the trapped gas more safely.

31
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:31,230
Today, Lake Nyos still exists.

32
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:33,030
Its waters look peaceful.

33
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:35,090
Its surroundings are beautiful.

34
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:38,290
But underneath that calm
surface once hid one

35
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:42,070
of the deadliest natural
surprises in modern history.

36
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,450
File One, The Unknown File.

